  "question": {
    "text": "Calculate the amount of calcium oxide (in grams) required when it reacts with 852 g of P<sub>4</sub>O<sub>10</sub>."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1008",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math> <mrow> <mn>6</mn> <mtext>CaO</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mtext>P</mtext> <mn>4</mn> </msub> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </msub> <mo>⟶</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mtext>Ca</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <msub> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>PO</mtext> <mn>4</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math><br />1 Mole P<sub>4</sub>O<sub>10</sub> = 284 g/mole<br />Moles of P<sub>4</sub>O<sub>10</sub> = <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>8</mn> <mn>5</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mn>8</mn> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> = 3 moles<br />Moles of CaO = 18 moles<br />Mass of CaO = 18 x 56 = 1008 g"
  }
